# Electromagnetic CGS units (EMU), from NIST SP 811 (2008), appendix B.8, and J. D. Jackson, Classical
# Electrodynamics, 3rd ed., appendix on units. Exact conversion factors to the SI units of the standard
# quantity types (F7: no new dimensions); the oersted is 1000/(4 pi) A/m and the gilbert 10/(4 pi) A.
# Format: symbol:name formula [Type]; '#' starts a comment.

@system EMU
@extends cgs.units
@include si.units

abA:abampere 10 A [ElectricCurrent]
abC:abcoulomb 10 C [ElectricCharge]
abV:abvolt 1e-8 V [ElectricPotential]
abΩ:abohm 1e-9 Ω [ElectricResistance]
abF:abfarad 1e9 F [ElectricCapacitance]
abH:abhenry 1e-9 H [ElectricInductance]
G:gauss 1e-4 T [MagneticFluxDensity]
Mx:maxwell 1e-8 Wb [MagneticFlux]
Gb:gilbert 2.5 pi^-1 A [ElectricCurrent]

# Magnetic field strength has no standard quantity type
Oe:oersted 250 pi^-1 A / m

@prefixed G m µ n

@preferred ElectricCharge abC
@preferred ElectricCurrent abA
@preferred ElectricPotential abV
@preferred ElectricResistance abΩ
@preferred ElectricCapacitance abF
@preferred ElectricInductance abH
@preferred MagneticFluxDensity G
@preferred MagneticFlux Mx
